@startuml 01-ticks-regular
title Geonera Ingestion — 1. Ticks Regular (T-0 / T-1 / T-2)
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #1B1B1B
skinparam ArrowColor #546E7A
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #1B1B1B
  FontSize 13

  BackgroundColor<<lock>> #EF6C00
  FontColor<<lock>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<lock>> #A34B00

  BackgroundColor<<db>> #1565C0
  FontColor<<db>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<db>> #0B3C78

  BackgroundColor<<r2>> #2E7D32
  FontColor<<r2>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<r2>> #1B5E20

  BackgroundColor<<api>> #AD1457
  FontColor<<api>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<api>> #6A0F38
}

skinparam activityDiamond {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3CD
  BorderColor #C79100
  FontColor #5D4037
}

skinparam legend {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #90A4AE
  FontColor #1B1B1B
  FontSize 12
  EntrySeparatorColor #CFD8DC
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #3E3E3E
}

legend right
  |= Tag |= Meaning |
  |<back:#EF6C00><color:#FFFFFF> lock </color></back>| Advisory-lock / Parent Handler step |
  |<back:#1565C0><color:#FFFFFF> db </color></back>| PostgreSQL transaction (state / outbox) |
  |<back:#2E7D32><color:#FFFFFF> r2 </color></back>| Cloudflare R2 storage I/O |
  |<back:#AD1457><color:#FFFFFF> api </color></back>| External Dukascopy API call |
endlegend

start
:runTickParentHandler(ctx, "REGULAR", dal);<<lock>>
note right
  Triggered by queue jobs.ticks.regular,
  expected to fire every hour at minute :05 (e.g. 10:05 UTC).
  Runs only after LockIDTick (1001) is acquired
  via the Direct Connection (see 00-overview-and-locking.puml).
end note

split
  ' ===================== T-0 =====================
  :**T-0 — Current Hour (Real-time Ingestion)**
  Target timestamp = current running hour
  (e.g. run at 10:05 -> target 10:00:00 UTC);
  :Claim: JobType=TICK, Status=PENDING,
  Instrument.IsPause=false & IsActive=true
  (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED via DAL.ExecuteInPool);
  :Update -> PROCESSED
  (SetPreviousStatus = old status, atomic);
  :Download raw BI5 file from Dukascopy API;<<api>>
  note right: Bounded Semaphore — hard cap **12** concurrent goroutines\n(primary defense against HTTP 429 Too Many Requests)
  :Convert BI5 integer format -> Parquet
  (Decimal/BigInt, using Instrument.Divider);
  note right: CPU-bound; runs outside the 12-slot limiter\nbut still guarded by a **separate** Bounded Semaphore (e.g. max 50)
  :Upload the resulting Parquet file to
  Cloudflare R2 (ticks/{instrument}/{YYYY}/{MM}/...);<<r2>>
  note right: I/O-bound; shares the same 50-slot semaphore\nas the convert step to keep RAM usage stable

  if (ETL Result?) then (Success)
    :Status -> COMPLETED;
  elseif () then (Source returns 404 / no data)
    :AddNotFoundStreak(+1) — atomic SQL increment
    (never read-modify-write in Go memory);
    if (NotFoundStreak >= 3 ?) then (yes)
      :Build Zero-Row Parquet in memory;
      :Atomically update DB: IsHoliday = true
      **(must commit BEFORE uploading to R2)**;
      :Upload Zero-Row Parquet to R2;<<r2>>
      :Status -> CONFIRMED;
    else (not yet)
      :Status -> NOT_FOUND;
    endif
  elseif () then (Handled error: network/system)
    :Status -> FAILED;
  else (Unhandled panic / crash mid-flight)
    :Row stays PROCESSED (stuck);
    note right: Will be swept up later by\nT-1 (Regular) or Backfill Reset Group
  endif

split again
  ' ===================== T-1 =====================
  :**T-1 — Previous Hour (Recovery & Retry / Safety Net)**
  Target timestamp = one hour before current
  (e.g. run at 10:05 -> target 09:00:00 UTC);
  :Claim: Status IN (PENDING, PROCESSED, FAILED, NOT_FOUND),
  Instrument.IsPause=false & IsActive=true;

  if (Claimed row's status?) then (PROCESSED — stuck/zombie worker)
    :Sweep & reset directly -> PENDING
    (no RetryCount change for TICK);
  elseif () then (PENDING)
    :Refresh / remains PENDING;
  elseif () then (FAILED)
    :AddRetryCount(+1) — atomic;
    if (RetryCount >= 5 ?) then (yes)
      :Status -> ABANDONED
      (prevents infinite retry loop,
      requires manual engineer intervention);
    else (no)
      :Status -> PENDING (will be retried);
    endif
  else (NOT_FOUND)
    if (Re-checking source: data now available?) then (yes — was just delayed)
      :Reset NotFoundStreak = 0 — atomic;
      :Status -> PENDING (re-attempt ingestion);
    else (still empty)
      :AddNotFoundStreak(+1) — atomic;
      if (NotFoundStreak >= 3 ?) then (yes — confirmed permanent holiday)
        :**Strict ordered Zero-Row procedure**
        (T-1 takes over autonomously to avoid
        partial-failure loops):
        1. Build Zero-Row Parquet in memory
        2. Update DB IsHoliday=true FIRST (atomic commit)
        3. Upload Zero-Row Parquet to R2
        4. Read back & physically validate (6.3)
        5. Status -> CONFIRMED + insert SyncTask (outbox);<<db>>
      else (still within tolerance)
        :Status remains NOT_FOUND;
      endif
    endif
  endif

split again
  ' ===================== T-2 =====================
  :**T-2 — Two Hours Ago (Physical Validation & Promotion)**
  Target timestamp = two hours before current
  (e.g. run at 10:05 -> target 08:00:00 UTC);
  :Claim: Status = COMPLETED,
  Instrument.IsActive = true;
  note right
    T-2 ONLY validates already-uploaded files —
    it never downloads from Dukascopy, and it
    never touches stray PROCESSED rows
    (that is exclusively Reset/Backfill's job).
  end note
  :Read the Parquet object directly from
  Cloudflare R2 (no re-download from source);<<r2>>
  :Run **Physical Parquet Validation** (criteria 6.3):
  - File existence & size > 0
  - Magic number PAR1 + footer integrity
  - Schema matching (columns, types, precision)
  - Data continuity & 1-hour boundary check
    (zero-row rows are valid only if IsHoliday=true);

  if (Validation result?) then (PASSED)
    :Status -> CONFIRMED (terminal / final);
    :Insert SyncTask (outbox event) in the
    **same DB transaction** as the status update,
    to keep ResolvedTickCount in sync;<<db>>
  else (FAILED — corrupt / schema mismatch / bad boundary)
    :Status -> BROKEN
    (queued for re-ingestion via Backfill,
    Overwrite Policy applies on retry);
    if (PreviousStatus == CONFIRMED ?) then (yes — demotion case)
      :Also insert a demotion SyncTask
      transactionally, to trigger
      ResolvedTickCount recompute;<<db>>
    endif
  endif
end split

:wg.Done() x3 — join point
(Parent Handler's wg.Wait() can now
proceed to release the advisory lock);
stop

@enduml
